{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A sixth identical call that hangs delays loop detection until another event or timeout, leaving the invocation running despite the required call count."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After the earlier result is evicted from the window, a changed polling result is counted as a repeat and can stop the agent prematurely."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When identical parallel calls finish out of order, the detector can abort the agent before distinct results reveal progress."}]}